From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haseenesss <Haseenesss@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:22:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Present snapshots: a texture is the game's again once its
 copy has run

With present snapshots on (Frame buffering, DM_PRESENT_SNAP), a present
that took a snapshot returned ticket 0, so the game's next acquire of that
texture waited for nothing and only the next ring slot paced it. The ring
slot is counted per present, not per texture: with more slots than
swapchain textures, or a game that acquires its next texture before it
presents the current frame, the game ran more frames ahead of the GPU than
its swapchain allows. Xenoblade Chronicles 3 keeps its CPU-written
per-frame uniform blocks in a ring sized on the swapchain and the GPU reads
them from the shared pool when the draw runs, so it rewrote a queued
frame's data: the 3D scene came out one flat colour, a new one each time,
under a correct HUD. Field walk on an M2, 80 screen captures each:
2 slots 32/80 and 4 slots 49/80 before, 0/80 and 0/80 after; snapshots off
0/80 either way.

A snapshot present now keeps its ticket, and the acquire of its texture
(nvn_queue_present_wait) waits in mtl_present_wait_texture until that
snapshot's copy has signalled g_snap_ev. The frame drawn into the texture
ran before the copy, so the game never has more frames in flight than its
swapchain holds, and it still does not wait for the screen, which is what
snapshots are for.

t_present_snap ticket checks it with 4 ring slots and 2 window textures:
the presents keep their tickets, acquiring a texture again waits for its
copy, and an acquire whose copy is held behind a GPU gate returns only once
the gate opens. Before the fix three of its checks fail. The test file also
renames nvn_mtl.m's weak nvn_hle_teardown in its translation unit, which
hle_nvn.c defines: t_present_snap did not compile at this pin.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#2153
Reason: Frame buffering (present snapshots) let Xenoblade Chronicles 3 rewrite per-frame data still in use: flat-colour frames
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1117

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
